<title>USA: GM expects 1.3 pct increase in '98 cars-WSJ.</title>
<headline>GM expects 1.3 pct increase in '98 cars-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp is expected to increase the average price for its 1998 models by 1.3 percent, the smallest increase in the past decade, the Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>General Motors is expected to announce the sticker prices later today for the next model year, which begins October 1. It will be the first of the U.S. big three automakers to announce the new prices.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
